{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd7f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ffe-0d1f-7ed2-b330-e35e6f06a0ee"},"sequence":1306,"recorded_at":1780531400002607,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f683aec3-8d4a-44b0-bdc9-05bef3ee2f1b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f683aec3-8d4a-44b0-bdc9-05bef3ee2f1b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f683aec3-8d4a-44b0-bdc9-05bef3ee2f1b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"2add5d4b-3a4d-4fbc-b9d4-e741d9d51a55"},"task_id":"2add5d4b-3a4d-4fbc-b9d4-e741d9d51a55","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"2add5d4b-3a4d-4fbc-b9d4-e741d9d51a55","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-45-1\",\n  \"command\": \"date +\\\"%H%M\\\"; head -n 20 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check time and logbook head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"0926\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-05\\n\\n### 0830 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-5 rework: the 28 real survivors, closed by derivation\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-4 verdict (changes requested, 106 mutants, 76 killed, 30 survived, 2 stated bounds, 28 real). Test-only rework in `internal/provhost` plus one comment restatement; production untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1, blocking): the eight closed vocabularies the three existing specdoc derivations did not cover are now derived the same way in `internal/provhost/closed_vocabularies_test.go` — probe statuses and evidence from the Section 7.4 sentences, architectures from 7.4 prose cross-checked against the 7.5 probe request row, probe platforms from that row (sorted both sides: the row lists macos first, the implementation holds sorted order), quiesce blockers from the 7.5 enum sentence, identity kinds from the 5.5 table row, identify confidence and matched-evidence from the 7.5 identify-session row. Each widening mutant from the verdict battery (partial, assumed, 386, freebsd, other, legacy_alias, guess, guessed) is killed twice: once by the derivation equality, once by an exact-member refusal row through the production entry point.\\n- FIX (F2): last-element substitution rows for both manifest order loops, first-element-unknown platform row (aix, still sorted-unique so it reaches the vocab check), and first/last missing-registry-key probe rows.\\n- FIX (F3): NUL-injection fixtures for both SpawnPlan members that reach exec — argv element and env-literal value — via JSON `\\\\u0000` escapes.\\n- FIX (F4): identity provider-correlation now pinned with the equal-length claude/gemini pair (both 6), with a length-equality guard so the fixture cannot go blind silently.\\n- FIX (F5): all ten bound+1 rows plus exactness acceptances on both sides (including the first SP8 fixture on either side: 65537 refused, 65536 accepted). LESSON: a bound+1 mutant is killed only by bound+1 exactly — the first SP8 draft totalled 69,632 bytes, above even the widened bound, and survived. Same class as the token-floor finding: the obligation must carry the literal.\\n- FIX (F6): aliasing tests for both copy guarantees (`MutationOperations`, `Capabilities`); the quiesce safe-rule comment restated to name backgroundNull as folded into !background by `rawNullableBool` (unreachable, not untested); the vacuous `runner.spawned() != 0` assertion on a Runner never handed to `RequireCapability` removed and restated as structural.\\n- BONUS: the manifest digit-first provider-id row also kills MA8, which the verdict battery listed as killed but is now pinned at the manifest layer too.\\n- ANOMALY: the first NUL-row draft wrote raw NUL bytes into the Go source (binary file, invalid-JSON refusal instead of the NUL arm); replaced with `\\\\u0000` escapes and verified zero NUL bytes remain. S1's ExecRunner fork/exec flake reappeared in 2 of ~30 full-package mutant runs; every affected mutant also failed its targeted test, so no verdict rests on it.\\n- EVIDENCE: 29-mutant replay (the 28 real survivors plus MA8) with the reviewer's own harness and spec files: 29 killed, 0 survived. `go build`, `go vet`, `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 15/15 green, provhost `-race` green, provhost cover 86.4% → 86.5%.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3494,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 874,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
