{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cda3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ffe-0d1f-7ed2-b330-e35e6f06a0ee"},"sequence":1324,"recorded_at":1780531400002643,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f683aec3-8d4a-44b0-bdc9-05bef3ee2f1b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f683aec3-8d4a-44b0-bdc9-05bef3ee2f1b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f683aec3-8d4a-44b0-bdc9-05bef3ee2f1b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"e319525d-80df-408a-9400-c76c7de273e0"},"task_id":"e319525d-80df-408a-9400-c76c7de273e0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"e319525d-80df-408a-9400-c76c7de273e0","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-05\n-\n-### 0830 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-5 rework: the 28 real survivors, closed by derivation\n+## 2026-09-05\n+\n+### 0926 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: the vocabulary class closed by census\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-5 verdict (changes requested, single blocking finding F1r). Test-only rework: new `internal/provhost/closed_vocabulary_census_test.go`, `requireVocabulary` comparison fix in `closed_vocabularies_test.go`. Production untouched; uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n+- FIX (F1r): the nine membership-checked vocabularies with no derivation (manifest/probe/capability/identity/identify/quiesce/spawn/status member sets plus the yolo mapping) are now derived from the pinned document — example-JSON keys for 7.3/7.4, first-sentence code spans for the capability-value sentence, TableRowAt Field rows for the 5.5 identity table, per-span member declarations for the 7.5 SpawnPlan/SafeBoundaryProof/ProviderTransactionStatus rows, braced-cell parsing for the identify-session success body, per-row provider-plus-first-flag for the 7.7 table. The census parses production source for package-level []string/map[string]bool/map[string]string with membership use (unknownMember argument, map index, range operand) and requires each of the 19 found vocabularies to carry an executing derivation, in both directions.\n+- EVIDENCE: probe_widen.json replay, full-package runs, cp+sha256 restores: W1–W9 KILLED (each red three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point refusal row), W10/R2/R4 killed, R1/R3 survive as the stated behaviour-preserving bounds. Fail-closed attacks all red: wrong type name, bad cell marker, off-table identity window, unregistered planted vocabulary (`has no registered spec derivation`), blinded string-map scan (`names no production vocabulary`), dropped registration. `requireVocabulary` now uses reflect.DeepEqual, so the V4 joined-member mutant is killed by the derivation alone. Gates: build/vet/GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 15/15 green, provhost -race green, provhost cover 86.5% unchanged.\n+- ANOMALY: the capability-value sentence shares its window with the warnings sentence, so a naive span read derives five members including warnings; the derivation truncates to the declaring sentence. The bare 5.5 closed sentence repeats in four sections, so the identity quote carries its schema opener to stay unique. The *Required order lists are excluded from the census by construction (missingMember-only use), which is what keeps R1/R3 surviving.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n+\n+### 0830 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-5 rework: the 28 real survivors, closed by derivation\n"}}}
